Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect usage of the `crtc` pointer in the `plane_state` structure when the `drm_device` could not be found. The original code attempted to access `plane_state->crtc->dev`, which could lead to a null pointer dereference if `crtc` was not valid. The fix involved changing the reference to `plane_state->plane->dev`, which is always valid, ensuring that the logging and error handling would function correctly even when the `crtc` was not available.
